label a0524:
    # --- Day 10: 2025-05-24 ---
    scene bg schoolgym
    $ show_calendar()
    show mood_afternoon zorder 3
    with dissolve_scene_full
    play music schooldays
    window auto
    "Saturday begins in the gym."
    "The whole student body has been arranged by year and class across the floor, standing in lines that look straight from a distance and start drifting the longer you look."
    "The teachers patrol the edges with clipboards and the faint exhaustion of people trying to keep several hundred students aligned."
    "{i}Morning pep assembly.{/i}"
    "{i}Because when a school says midterms begin Monday, apparently the next step is forced enthusiasm under fluorescent lighting.{/i}"
    "Somewhere near the front, a microphone pops."
    "\"Good morning, students.\""
    "The speakers answer with a feedback squeal sharp enough to make half the gym flinch."
    "{i}No one looks more encouraged afterward.{/i}"
    "\"As you know, midterm examinations begin after the weekend.\""
    "\"This assembly is a chance to remember that preparation, discipline, and mutual encouragement are the foundations of student success.\""
    "Several hundred teenagers absorb that with the patience of people who were told to stand before homeroom."
    "I end up with Asahina drifting back to my side and Sam one row behind me, because the lines have softened enough to make assigned order theoretical."
    show asahina neut at t31
    show sam neut at t32
    "Technically, Sam and I are both with the seniors; he's just in the row behind mine."
    "Practically, Asahina's class line has collapsed backward enough that she and Sam are close enough to keep talking without looking like they moved there on purpose."
    "Asahina's sleeve cuff has folded weirdly."
    "Sam notices before she does, reaches over, fixes it with two fingers, and steps back like nothing happened."
    "Asahina looks ahead harder than any person has ever looked ahead."
    ah "...Thanks."
    sa "Anytime."
    "{i}I am not prepared for how ordinary that looks.{/i}"
    "{i}A loud kind of cute would have been easier to mock. This is quiet enough that I have to notice it honestly.{/i}"
    mc "If you two get any more considerate, I'm transferring."
    ah "No one asked you to observe."
    sa "We can try to keep the consideration under control."
    ah "Do not enable him."
    "Sam smiles just enough to make Asahina's ears turn pink instead of making her defensive."
    "{i}He knows how much attention to give without making it a scene.{/i}"
    "\"You are not merely taking tests. You are proving the discipline you have built all term.\""
    "A classmate behind me mutters something about proving he built nothing and receiving his sentence accordingly."
    "I respect the honesty."
    "\"You may feel anxious. That is natural.\""
    "\"But anxiety is not an enemy. It is a signal that what you are doing matters.\""
    "{i}Or a signal that four subjects have been quietly circling my weekend with paperwork.{/i}"
    "The speech keeps going."
    "Goals. Community. Study habits. Sleep. Hydration. The usual checklist."
    "Coach stands near the wall with his arms folded, and even from here I can tell he is mentally underlining hydration."
    "A projector screen at the side of the stage displays a slogan in clean blue letters:"
    "{i}YOUR EFFORT TODAY BECOMES TOMORROW'S CONFIDENCE.{/i}"
    "{i}My confidence tomorrow will be a half-dead mechanical pencil and whatever notes survived my backpack.{/i}"
    "Asahina shifts her weight."
    "Sam shifts with her a fraction later, casual enough that it could be coincidence if I had not started noticing these things against my will."
    mc "If I pass out, tell them the assembly did it."
    ah "If you pass out, I'm taking your lunch."
    sa "I would probably tell someone first."
    ah "I didn't say I wouldn't tell someone. I said I'd take his lunch."
    mc "Good to know."
    "Sam laughs softly."
    "It is a good laugh, not too loud and not too careful, letting the joke land without stealing it."
    "{i}That is what I mean. Too calm to dismiss, which is inconvenient in a different way.{/i}"
    "The assembly reaches the part where the student council representative thanks everyone for their attention, despite the room offering little proof."
    "Bodies begin preparing to move before permission arrives."
    "Shoes adjust. Bags rustle. Someone coughs like the speech has personally wronged him."
    "\"Remember: Monday is not a wall. It is a step.\""
    "{i}It can be both, actually.{/i}"
    "The microphone clicks off."
    "The gym exhales in one enormous, adolescent wave."
    "Teachers start directing classes toward the exits before the whole room moves at once."
    show asahina neut at t41
    show sam neut at t42
    show tsubaki neut at t43
    "Tsubaki appears at the edge of our row with a notebook hugged to her chest and a look of immediate apology."
    ts "Sorry, excuse me..."
    ts "I think my class is cutting through here."
    ah "Oh, Tsubaki!"
    "Tsubaki looks up, startled by being recognized and then relieved that the recognition has a friendly source."
    ts "Oh. Hi, Asahina. [player]."
    mc "Morning."
    "Her gaze flicks to Sam."
    "Not long -- barely even enough to qualify as a glance."
    "But she notices him the way people notice a door they might need to pass through."
    ah "This is Sam."
    "The phrase comes out casual, then spends half a second trying not to sound proud."
    ah "My, uh..."
    sa "Boyfriend."
    "He supplies it gently enough that it does not corner her."
    ah "...Yeah. That."
    "Tsubaki's hands tighten around the notebook, only a little."
    ts "Oh! Right. Nice to meet you."
    sa "Masayami Inugami."
    sa "Sam's fine, though."
    ts "Tsubaki Kareda."
    "She bows just enough to be polite, and the loose sheet tucked inside her notebook slips forward."
    "Sam catches it before it can hit the floor."
    "Again, too smooth to look practiced unless someone is already watching for the practice."
    sa "Got it."
    ts "Ah--thank you."
    "He hands it back without looking at the writing."
    "Or he looks so quickly that it does not register as looking."
    sa "Your name was on the poster note, right?"
    ts "Poster note?"
    sa "Asahina told me someone actually gave useful feedback on the volleyball poster."
    "Asahina's head snaps toward him."
    ah "I did not say it like that."
    sa "You said, and I quote, 'she understood the motion lines, which means she has functioning eyes and taste.'"
    ah "That quote is sealed evidence."
    mc "Too late. Entered into the record."
    "Tsubaki lowers her eyes toward the sheet like it might hide her face if she believes hard enough."
    ts "It was just a nice poster."
    sa "Still. Good eye."
    "The compliment is small."
    "The impact is not."
    "Tsubaki's delayed smile starts, panics, and becomes something she stores safely behind a nod."
    ts "Thanks."
    "A teacher claps twice near the doorway."
    "\"Second-years, keep moving.\""
    ts "I should go."
    ah "Yeah, before the crowd seals the path."
    ts "That sounds more tactical than I expected."
    mc "School traffic has strategy."
    "Tsubaki smiles for real this time, quick and almost surprised by itself."
    ts "See you later."
    sa "Later, Kareda."
    "Her step catches by half a beat."
    "Then she moves with her class."
    show tsubaki at thide
    hide tsubaki
    show asahina neut at t21
    show sam neut at t22
    "Asahina watches her go with a neutral expression that is trying to decide what category the interaction belongs in."
    ah "...She's nice."
    mc "You said that yesterday."
    ah "Maybe she's still nice today. Ever think of that?"
    sa "She seems careful."
    "Careful is a clean word."
    "Too clean, maybe."
    "Asahina looks at him."
    ah "Careful how?"
    sa "Like she thinks being noticed and being in the way are the same thing."
    "That's more accurate than I want it to be."
    "Even Asahina does not immediately joke over it."
    ah "...Yeah."
    "{i}Huh.{/i}"
    "{i}He noticed that from thirty seconds?{/i}"
    "{i}Good eye, indeed.{/i}"
    "The traffic behind us begins to push."
    mc "Okay, we should move before the gym decides we live here now."
    ah "Dramatic."
    sa "A little accurate, though."
    "We move with the crowd, and the assembly disappears behind us with the hard plastic smell of the gym floor."
    show asahina at thide
    hide asahina
    show sam at thide
    hide sam
    $ hide_calendar()
    scene black with wipeleft_scene
    nier "The school day resumes with less inspiration than advertised."
    nier "Homeroom becomes a distribution center for exam reminders. Civics becomes another warning about definitions. Language arts tells us restraint is important, which feels personally targeted after the gym trapped us all in a motivational speech."
    nier "By the time college algebra arrives, my notebook has already begun to look like evidence of a quiet emergency."
    call nier_clear from _call_nier_clear_0524_1
    scene bg class_day
    $ show_calendar()
    show mood_afternoon zorder 3
    stop music fadeout 1.0
    with wipeleft_scene
    play music quiz
    "College algebra review begins with the particular silence only matrices can create."
    "There is a grid on the board."
    "Then another grid."
    "Then arrows, brackets, and enough numbers to suggest the teacher has stopped believing in mercy."
    show math_teacher neut at t11
    math_teacher "Matrices are not decorative boxes."
    math_teacher "They are a way to organize operations."
    math_teacher "If you treat them like a pile of numbers wearing brackets, you will make mistakes that are very easy to avoid."
    "{i}Decorative boxes. Got it.{/i}"
    "The teacher writes two matrices on the board."
    "{i}A is two by three. B is three by two.{/i}"
    math_teacher "First check: can AB be multiplied?"
    "Several students look down, which is the international classroom signal for please let this question choose someone else."
    "I make the fatal mistake of having already written the dimensions in my notes."
    math_teacher "[player]."
    mc "...Yes?"
    math_teacher "Can AB be multiplied, and what size is the result?"
    show mood_pressure zorder 4
    show vignette zorder 5 at ambient_vignette(0.24)
    with dissolve
    "{i}Ah, matrices. Organized numbers and public consequences.{/i}"
    menu:
        "Yes. The result is two by two.":
            hide mood_pressure
            hide vignette
            with dissolve
            mc "Yes. The inside dimensions match, so the result takes the outside dimensions."
            mc "Two by two."
            math_teacher "Correct."
            "He circles the three and three in the middle, then boxes the two and two on the outside."
            math_teacher "Inside confirms compatibility. Outside gives the result."
            "{i}A sentence simple enough to make Monday feel a little less hostile.{/i}"
        "Yes. The result is three by three.":
            hide mood_pressure
            hide vignette
            with dissolve
            mc "Yes, and..."
            "The board stares back."
            "The two and two sit outside the expression like they are waiting for me to stop embarrassing both of us."
            mc "...Nope. Two by two. Inside checks, outside tells."
            math_teacher "Good correction."
            math_teacher "The result uses the outside dimensions. Do not average the sizes, do not guess by vibes, and do not let panic do arithmetic."
            "{i}Panic is not a reliable calculator. Noted.{/i}"
        "No. The dimensions do not match.":
            hide mood_pressure
            hide vignette
            with dissolve
            mc "No, because..."
            "I stop before the sentence can run directly into traffic."
            "Two by three times three by two."
            "The middle dimensions match."
            mc "...Actually yes. The result is two by two."
            math_teacher "Caught it. Good."
            math_teacher "Check the inner dimensions before deciding. The outside dimensions give the final size."
            "{i}Nearly taken out by a bracket. Not my proudest moment.{/i}"
    math_teacher "Now BA."
    "The board receives a second set of arrows."
    math_teacher "Order matters."
    math_teacher "AB and BA are not guaranteed to have the same size, the same value, or even both exist."
    "{i}Order matters. Math apparently has social boundaries too.{/i}"
    "He writes a multiplication table step by step."
    "Row times column."
    "Row one, column one. Row one, column two. Then repeat."
    "It is tedious in the way that makes mistakes feel insulting when they happen."
    math_teacher "Midterm expectation: you must show the setup."
    math_teacher "If I see a correct answer with no path, I cannot tell whether you understood it or rolled lucky dice."
    "{i}Tough but fair.{/i}"
    "{i}Also a clean attack against my occasional strategy of writing the answer and hoping the method looks implied.{/i}"
    "The class practices three examples."
    "By the second one, the room has settled into scratchy pencil noise and low-grade despair."
    "By the third, someone near the windows asks whether calculators will be allowed and receives a look normally reserved for betrayal."
    math_teacher "Calculators can multiply numbers. They cannot save you from entering the wrong structure."
    "That becomes another sentence everyone writes down because it sounds enough like a warning to deserve ink."
    show math_teacher at thide
    hide math_teacher
    $ hide_calendar()
    scene black with wipeleft_scene
    nier "Algebra finishes with a review sheet heavy enough to change the weather in my bag."
    nier "Chemistry and English both add their own papers to the stack, because Saturday apparently has no interest in staying light."
    nier "The assembly slogan returns to me while I stuff everything into my bag. Today's effort becomes tomorrow's confidence."
    nier "At the moment, today's effort has mostly become shoulder strain."
    call nier_clear from _call_nier_clear_0524_2
    scene bg corridor
    $ show_calendar()
    show mood_afternoon zorder 3
    stop music fadeout 1.0
    with wipeleft_scene
    play music dailyfantasy
    "Lunch arrives late enough to feel hypothetical."
    "The corridor is loud with Saturday relief, exam dread, and the specific disbelief of students who cannot believe they had to attend a pep assembly for tests."
    show asahina neut at t11
    "Asahina finds me by the stairwell."
    ah "Roof?"
    mc "You've really streamlined the invitation process."
    ah "Roof, please."
    mc "Powerful revision."
    "She glances down the hall once."
    mc "Where's Sam?"
    ah "Senior thing."
    ah "Or basketball thing. Or both. He said he'd text me after."
    "The answer is casual enough to pass if I were not legally related to her."
    mc "You sound normal about it."
    ah "I'm normal about literally everything."
    mc "Your dedication is moving."
    ah "Roof or no roof?"
    mc "Roof."
    show asahina at thide
    hide asahina
    $ hide_calendar()
    scene black with wipeleft_scene
    scene bg rooftop
    $ show_calendar()
    show mood_afternoon zorder 3
    with wipeleft_scene
    play sound moddooropen
    "The rooftop air feels less recycled than the rest of the building, which is enough to make it valuable."
    "The sky has that washed Saturday brightness that makes everything below it look like it should have been released from school hours ago."
    show asahina neut at t11
    "Asahina sits against the wall and opens her lunch with the speed of someone trying not to check her phone."
    "She checks her phone immediately after."
    mc "Subtle."
    ah "I'm checking the time."
    mc "On a screen with a heart sticker near the camera."
    ah "That sticker was free."
    "She points her chopsticks at me without looking up, ears going faintly pink."
    ah "Eat your food."
    "I obey, partly because she is right and partly because I am hungry enough to stop arguing."
    "The first few minutes are quiet."
    "Not awkward quiet -- just the sibling kind that exists because neither of us believes silence means the relationship has crashed."
    "Asahina finally puts the phone facedown on her lunch bag."
    ah "Do you think Tsubaki was okay earlier?"
    mc "In the gym?"
    ah "No, in the ocean. Yes, in the gym."
    "I take a second longer than usual to answer."
    mc "She seemed...Tsubaki."
    ah "That means nothing."
    mc "It means careful, apologetic, and surprised when somebody says a nice thing to her."
    ah "Yeah."
    "Asahina pokes at her food."
    ah "Sam said good eye, and she looked like he handed her an award."
    mc "You jealous?"
    "Her head turns very slowly."
    ah "Don't be stupid."
    mc "Okay."
    "The easy joke waits in front of me."
    "I leave it there."
    "Asahina keeps her eyes on the skyline."
    ah "It's just...I dunno."
    ah "I get how nice compliments feel when you don't expect them."
    "The poster hangs between the words without being named."
    mc "...Yeah."
    "My phone buzzes before the sentence can decide whether to keep breathing."
    "Monika."
    python:
        _phone_messages = [
            phone_msg("them", "Where did you disappear to?"),
            phone_msg("them", "I checked the club room for a second and it was aggressively empty."),
            phone_msg("me", "Roof. Asa pulled rank for lunch."),
            phone_msg("them", "Kidnapped? Should I notify someone?"),
            phone_msg("me", "No, she has snacks. Negotiations are stable."),
            phone_msg("them", "Good. Stay there for a few minutes? I wanted to ask you something before afternoon classes."),
            phone_msg("me", "Sure. Door's unlocked, probably."),
        ]
    call phone_text_conversation("Monika", _phone_messages, append=True) from _call_phone_text_conversation_0524_1
    ah "Monika?"
    mc "Yeah."
    ah "Wow. She came looking?"
    mc "She wants to ask something."
    ah "Uh huh."
    mc "That's all I know."
    ah "Uh huh."
    mc "Can you not make that noise like you solved something?"
    ah "Can you not be suspicious on school property?"
    "The rooftop door opens."
    play sound moddooropen
    show asahina neut at t21
    show monika 1a at t22
    "Monika steps out with a folder against her chest and wind immediately pulling at the loose ribbon of her bow."
    m "There you are."
    mc "Present."
    ah "Mostly."
    m "Hi, Asahina."
    ah "Yo."
    "Asahina's yo is the exact kind of casual she uses when she is aware of being evaluated and refuses to give the room that much power."
    "Monika either does not notice or is polite enough to let her keep it."
    m "Sorry to interrupt lunch."
    ah "You're not. I was about to return to civilization anyway."
    mc "You were?"
    ah "Yes. Because I am responsible and have..."
    "Her phone buzzes once under her lunch bag."
    ah "...a thing."
    mc "A senior thing? Basketball thing?"
    ah "A leaving thing."
    "She packs with a speed that fails to look innocent."
    ah "Later."
    m "See you."
    mc "Be normal responsibly."
    ah "Handle your request responsibly."
    show asahina at thide
    hide asahina
    play sound moddoorclose
    "The door closes behind her."
    "The roof is suddenly much quieter."
    show monika 1a at t11
    "Monika remains standing for a second, fingers tightening around the folder."
    "That is new."
    "Not the folder. Monika always has some form of paper nearby, as if stationery quietly reproduces in her bag."
    "The tightening."
    mc "You good?"
    m "Yeah."
    m "I just wanted to ask before I talked myself into making it overly responsible."
    mc "Concerning phrase."
    "She laughs once, soft and not quite enough."
    m "Tomorrow's our last full study day before exams."
    m "I know you probably already have a plan, and I know your science and math stuff is more...you know."
    mc "Soul-crushing?"
    m "STEM-oriented."
    mc "Diplomatic."
    m "I try."
    "She sits beside me, leaving a careful space that feels more deliberate than sitting close would."
    m "I was thinking we could meet at the public library in the morning."
    m "Study for a few hours, trade notes where we can, maybe quiz each other."
    m "I can help with language arts and civics, you can help me not get destroyed by algebra notation, and we can both pretend biology is a normal subject."
    mc "Bold plan."
    m "After that, if we survive, there's that new cafe downtown in the historic district."
    m "The one with the green awning near the old bank building."
    "She looks down at the folder."
    "A corner of a printed review sheet peeks out."
    m "I thought lunch there might be nice."
    "The word nice arrives without decoration."
    "It does more damage that way."
    "{i}Ah.{/i}"
    "{i}So not only studying, then.{/i}"
    "Monika keeps talking before the silence can become too visible."
    m "Not as, like, a big thing."
    m "Just..."
    m "Exams are coming up. Track is back. The club has been a little scattered. You have college stuff now, and your family, and..."
    "She stops herself there."
    "For a second, the president version of Monika disappears."
    "Not dramatically -- just enough for the person underneath to look out and see whether the request is too much."
    m "I missed talking to you without the school day pulling at our sleeves."
    "I look at the city beyond the fence."
    "The assembly slogan has left my head."
    "The matrix review sheet has stopped rustling in my bag."
    "There is only Monika, the rooftop wind, and the awkward responsibility of answering without sanding the sentence down into a joke."
    mc "Yeah."
    mc "Library sounds good."
    mc "Cafe too."
    "She looks up."
    m "Really?"
    mc "Really."
    mc "I mean, I was probably going to spend the morning arguing with notes anyway."
    mc "Might as well do that with someone who can tell me when my explanation stops sounding like a sentence."
    "Her shoulders loosen."
    m "That's one of my core talents."
    mc "Your marketable skills are terrifying."
    m "Thank you."
    "The smile returns, but smaller."
    "Earned, maybe."
    m "I'll send you the time tonight."
    mc "I can meet you there at, like, nine."
    m "Nine works."
    m "Don't make me text five reminders."
    mc "I would never."
    m "You absolutely would, by needing them."
    mc "Cruel and partially correct."
    "The warning bell rings below us, thin and distant."
    "Monika stands first."
    m "Okay. I should get back before the faculty starts wondering."
    mc "Reasonable."
    m "Occasionally."
    "She pauses near the door."
    m "Thanks."
    mc "For saying yes?"
    m "For not making me make it smaller."
    "That one takes the air out of my joke before it forms."
    mc "...Yeah."
    mc "No problem."
    "Monika gives me one more look, then slips back inside."
    show monika at thide
    hide monika
    play sound moddoorclose
    "The rooftop goes back to wind and concrete."
    "My lunch is almost finished."
    "The day is not."
    $ update_character_thought("monika", "Monika asked for Sunday at the library with enough careful framing that studying almost sounded like the excuse.")
    $ hide_calendar()
    scene black with wipeleft_scene
    nier "Afternoon classes take the rooftop away."
    nier "Chemistry finishes the last review packet with no regard for human limits. English hands back vocabulary sheets. Homeroom ends with one more announcement about pencils, student IDs, and the moral necessity of sleeping before an exam."
    nier "By the final bell, the school feels less like a building and more like a machine ejecting tired students into the weekend."
    call nier_clear from _call_nier_clear_0524_3
    scene bg club_day
    $ show_calendar()
    show mood_afternoon zorder 3
    stop music fadeout 1.0
    with wipeleft_scene
    play music daily
    "The club room is warmer than usual when I arrive -- not physically, though the afternoon sun does its best."
    "A few members are already there, notebooks open and chairs pulled into loose corners, but the room has settled into a rare quiet."
    show monika 1a at t11
    "Monika stands near the board, writing the prompt in clean letters."
    "{i}Write about a place where pressure changes shape.{/i}"
    "Monika turns when she hears the door."
    m "Hey."
    mc "Hey."
    "The word is normal."
    "Unfortunately, lunch has made normal feel like it is carrying contraband."
    "I take my usual seat and pull out my notebook."
    "The desk has a tiny nick near the corner that my thumb finds before my brain does."
    "Same desk, same room."
    "A day can still make familiar things feel shifted by half an inch."
    m "I figured we could keep it low pressure today."
    "She glances back at the board and notices the wording."
    m "Relatively low pressure."
    mc "The prompt gets a pass."
    "Monika gives a small, tired smile."
    m "Fifteen minutes drafting, then voluntary exchange."
    m "And actually voluntary. Everyone looks tired enough that forcing feedback would just make the poems defensive."
    "The room lowers into writing."
    "For a while, there is only paper noise."
    "Someone near the back erases a line hard enough to wrinkle the page."
    "A desk creaks, then settles."
    "Monika writes steadily, pauses, crosses out exactly three words, and keeps going."
    "I stare at the prompt longer than I should."
    "{i}A place where pressure changes shape.{/i}"
    "The obvious answer is school."
    "The smarter answer is not to write the obvious answer if I do not want to sound like a motivational poster that learned resentment."
    "My pen moves before I fully decide."
    "{i}On the bus, the window turns the city into a strip of things I am allowed to leave behind.{/i}"
    "{i}Not forever. Just stop by stop.{/i}"
    "{i}Pressure becomes distance when the doors close.{/i}"
    "I stop."
    "Then I write the next line before I can overthink it."
    "{i}The seat remembers nobody, which is why it is kind.{/i}"
    "{i}No one asks whether I am doing well in the reflection.{/i}"
    "{i}It only carries my face until the glass gets too dark to give it back.{/i}"
    "I look at the lines."
    "{i}Not exactly the cheerful version of exam-week pressure, then.{/i}"
    "Across the room, Monika lifts her head like she can tell I have stopped at the unsafe part."
    m "You stopped."
    mc "For now."
    m "That sounded protective."
    mc "It probably was."
    "Monika stands and brings her notebook to my desk once the timer on her phone buzzes."
    show monika 1a at t11
    "The voluntary exchange becomes voluntary once Monika is standing there with her notebook."
    m "Trade?"
    mc "Yeah."
    "We swap notebooks."
    "Her handwriting is neater than mine even when she is drafting."
    "The title is crossed out."
    "Under it, a new one sits in smaller letters."
    "{i}Table Near The Window{/i}"
    "I read."
    "{i}A review sheet lies open between two cups.{/i}"
    "{i}One cup is mine because lipstick makes ownership legible.{/i}"
    "{i}The other is his because he keeps turning it by the rim when he does not know where to put a thought.{/i}"
    "{i}Outside, buses practice leaving.{/i}"
    "{i}Inside, I underline the same sentence twice so my hands have work.{/i}"
    "{i}Pressure changes shape when someone stays long enough to quiz you on the hard parts.{/i}"
    "I stop reading for a second."
    "The room keeps being the room."
    "A page turns somewhere behind us."
    "Someone asks a quiet question about whether a line is too blunt, and the answer comes back just as quietly."
    "Monika sits across from me, reading my six defensive lines with a focused expression."
    "It should be easy to say something."
    "It is not."
    mc "This is..."
    "Monika looks up."
    m "Too much?"
    mc "No."
    "The answer comes out faster than I expect."
    mc "No, it's good."
    mc "Specific."
    mc "It feels like the table exists."
    m "That was the hope."
    "She smiles, then looks back down at my notebook."
    m "Yours is good too."
    "She reads it once more, slower, and her finger stops near the margin where, on any other draft, there would be a bracket."
    "There isn't one."
    m "Huh. No brackets this time."
    mc "...Didn't need them."
    "She doesn't answer that. She just looks at me for a second, the way she did over a red pen the first week, and lets it be true."
